WEBVTT

00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:15.360
"I can't overcome it"  "I'm annoyed"

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:20.100
Even if I break down those hurdles

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:28.310
No answer emerges

00:00:28.310 --> 00:00:34.810
Am I being controlled?  Everyone on the field

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:39.750
Isn't scared, go away, but...

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:43.450
The unseen road to the future

00:00:43.450 --> 00:00:51.200
Cannot be chosen

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:54.500
Close your eyes and cut with your heart

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.160
just like cards, surely

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.230
It was promised  yes!  you are the winner

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:06.100
never lose!  Cut with your heart

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.330
just like cards, surely

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:16.680
Because a miracle will occur

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:24.230
Diamond Blade!

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.330
I'm done for!

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:33.130
The only monster I got into enemy territory is now destroyed.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:37.880
My opponent has three monsters and one unknown item.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:40.380
I only have three monsters.

00:01:41.290 --> 00:01:42.800
What should I do?

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.020
Miracle Dimension
Summon Dark Magician

00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:58.260
Dice roll!

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:04.170
Knight of Twin Swords's effect allows it to double its movement.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.140
It's my turn.

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:12.970
Will you make it in time, Yugi?

00:02:12.970 --> 00:02:14.710
My attacks are fast.

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.480
Dice roll!

00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:21.990
I move Orgoth the Relentless forward!

00:02:25.210 --> 00:02:28.280
Orgoth the Relentless is heading towards Warp Vortex!

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:29.680
That's right.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.930
It'll take the warp route to enter your territory quickly.

00:02:32.930 --> 00:02:34.280
Invade!

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.260
Orgoth the Relentless warps!

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:57.950
It's here!

00:02:57.950 --> 00:03:02.230
If I don't do something, Orgoth the Relentless will control my territory!

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.320
My turn!  Dice roll!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.510
I'll gather my monsters together to defend me!

00:03:12.710 --> 00:03:14.870
I move Thunder Ball!

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.370
I move Mighty Mage!

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.500
I move Knight of Twin Swords!

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.800
A wall of monsters can't stop Orgoth the Relentless!

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.650
It's my turn!

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:31.120
I move Orgoth the Relentless.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:36.560
I activate Orgoth the Relentless's effect.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.570
I use two Magic Crests to raise its attack points by 10, raising it to 40.

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.500
Orgoth the Relentless, attack Thunder Ball!

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.180
Diamond Blade!

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.920
That's all for now, Yugi.

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:03.370
Cool!

00:04:03.370 --> 00:04:05.360
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.790
Otogi has the advantage again.

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:12.690
He doesn't have enough monsters.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.130
Can he summon another one, Anzu?

00:04:15.130 --> 00:04:15.890
He can't.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:20.250
There's no space left in his territory to dimension his dice.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:26.230
Hang in there, Yugi.

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:30.180
Now is when a duelist's true strength is tested.

00:04:32.060 --> 00:04:37.490
Yugi, you only have two monsters left, and you can't summon anymore.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.200
For your first time playing this game, you did well.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.960
I applaud you.

00:04:44.040 --> 00:04:49.160
But you're no match for the great duelist Pegasus.

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.040
Don't be overconfident!

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:57.080
It's not over yet!

00:04:57.310 --> 00:04:58.740
It's my turn!

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:00.050
Dice roll!

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:06.130
You created this game, but you forgot something!

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.760
Mighty Mage can attack opponents two spaces away!

00:05:10.220 --> 00:05:13.290
Mighty Mage, Lightning Rod!

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:17.120
I'll use a Defense Crest against your magic attack!

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:20.500
Orgoth the Relentless, activate your defense!

00:05:23.770 --> 00:05:26.310
It deflected Mighty Mage's attack!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:34.030
Orgoth the Relentless takes 10 points of damage, lowering its hit points to 20.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:40.200
Orgoth the Relentless has 40 attack points, so Mighty Mage takes 20 damage.

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.900
But it still has 20 hit points left.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.250
It can still fight!

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:45.190
How naïve.

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.630
It's my turn.

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.820
Dice roll!

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:54.430
I move Orgoth the Relentless one space!

00:05:57.260 --> 00:05:59.800
Orgoth the Relentless has 40 attack points.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:05.810
Its effect lets me use six Magic Crests to raise its attack points by 30.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:11.890
Orgoth the Relentless's attack points increased from 40 to 70?

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.590
Even if I use a Defense Crest, it won't survive!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.030
Orgoth the Relentless attacks Mighty Mage!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.020
Super Diamond Blade!

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:29.060
I only have one monster left.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:32.200
I can't defend against his powerful monsters.

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:37.140
There's no way you can turn this match around.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.220
What should I do?

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:46.130
At this rate, I won't be able to use this game to make him understand.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.860
That's not all.

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.770
He'll take Duel Monsters away from my other self.

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.080
Are you surrendering, Yugi?

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:03.070
Yugi, roll the dice!

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:06.120
He talked again!

00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:07.340
When he's a dog!

00:07:07.340 --> 00:07:08.840
The nerve!

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:11.210
Be quiet!  I'll just say this!

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.880
Fight, Yugi!

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:18.590
I'm sorry, Jonouchi.

00:07:19.070 --> 00:07:21.580
I promised to free you, but...

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:24.010
I'm not asking you to fight for me!

00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:27.690
Fight for so many other duelists, Yugi!

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:29.970
For other duelists?

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:36.370
Yeah!  For the duelists who passionately fought with all their might and lost against you!

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.520
That's even true for Pegasus!

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:49.080
He used all his strength to try to crush you and was defeated!

00:07:52.960 --> 00:07:57.280
Even though it's a different game, if you're the king of Duel Monsters...

00:07:57.280 --> 00:08:03.930
...you have a responsibility to fight to the end for all those duelists you defeated!

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.170
That's right!

00:08:06.170 --> 00:08:07.430
That's right, Yugi!

00:08:07.430 --> 00:08:09.300
Act like the king to the end!

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.370
Well said, Jonouchi!

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:14.800
But your words aren't convincing when you're dressed liked a dog.

00:08:19.170 --> 00:08:21.370
Thank you, Jonouchi.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.800
I almost forgot my duty as a duelist.

00:08:25.800 --> 00:08:29.280
Cards and dice are different, but a game is a game.

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:34.740
I'll focus all my will on these dice, and I won't give up until the end.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:39.230
I'll protect my pride as the king of duelists!

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.880
That's right, Yugi.

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.740
That's why you're my grandson!

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:51.740
Here I go, partner.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.060
All right, dice roll!

00:09:13.220 --> 00:09:14.940
Dice roll!

00:09:20.420 --> 00:09:24.880
I use a Movement Crest to move Knight of Twin Swords two spaces.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:36.520
Then I can use two Attack Crests to allow it to attack a monster multiple times!

00:09:36.990 --> 00:09:39.690
Otogi has five Defense Crests.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:43.160
If I use all my crests, I'll be able to defeat it.

00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.630
Knight of Twin Swords!

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:50.340
I'll use all my Attack Crests to let it attack six times!

00:09:50.340 --> 00:09:53.640
Attack Orgoth the Relentless with six sword slashes!

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:56.970
Twin Sword Continuous Six Slash!

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.060
Don't underestimate me!

00:10:00.510 --> 00:10:03.180
I activate Yaranzo's effect!

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:08.140
It transforms three Trap Crests into a Defense Crest!

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.770
What?

00:10:21.770 --> 00:10:26.000
He withstood all six of Knight of Twin Swords's slashes?

00:10:26.350 --> 00:10:27.520
See that?

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:33.400
Yaranzo can change three crests in my crest pool into any crest that I want.

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:39.210
Your attacks didn't leave a scratch on Orgoth the Relentless.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:40.950
It's my turn.

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:42.820
Dice roll!

00:10:43.690 --> 00:10:47.950
Orgoth the Relentless, attack Knight of Twin Swords!

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:53.520
Orgoth the Relentless's attack points are too high!

00:10:53.820 --> 00:10:56.650
Defending won't do any good.

00:10:57.480 --> 00:10:59.630
Diamond Blade!

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.210
Yugi!

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.040
Knight of Twin Swords is destroyed!

00:11:09.040 --> 00:11:11.290
Your monsters are all destroyed.

00:11:11.290 --> 00:11:12.650
What will you do now?

00:11:13.350 --> 00:11:18.330
I have no monsters, but I still have two life points.

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:22.020
I won't give up this game until the very end!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:32.970
He doesn't have any space to dimension his dice, so his odds of summoning a monster is close to zero.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:37.140
But he's still not disheartened.

00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:38.400
Why?

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:41.840
I didn't know his spirit was so strong.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:48.220
There must be something I can do.

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.130
There's nothing you can do.

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.530
Give up and kneel before me.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:05.370
I move Orgoth the Relentless two spaces to reach the Dungeon Master!

00:12:09.650 --> 00:12:13.670
Orgoth the Relentless, attack Yugi the Dungeon Master!

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:30.280
If you don't defeat Orgoth the Relentless next turn, you lose.

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:35.500
But I give you credit for dropping Orgoth the Relentless's hit points to 20.

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:38.100
The battle isn't over yet!

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:42.170
I just have to summon a monster that can destroy Orgoth the Relentless!

00:12:42.170 --> 00:12:43.170
What?

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:46.870
You're still not giving up?

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:52.250
You don't have the space to summon a monster!

00:12:58.480 --> 00:13:00.050
Yugi...

00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:02.800
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:05.380
L-O-V-E Otogi!

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:09.370
Gaming fans around the world are watching on the internet.

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:13.430
Stop this pointless struggle and admit your defeat.

00:13:14.080 --> 00:13:15.680
I will win.

00:13:15.680 --> 00:13:22.080
I will create a miracle for Yugi and all other duelists!

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:25.250
Dice roll!

00:13:33.880 --> 00:13:38.040
You don't have the space in your territory to dimension the dice.

00:13:38.760 --> 00:13:40.440
Are you sure about that?

00:13:40.440 --> 00:13:41.160
What?

00:13:41.240 --> 00:13:45.720
Otogi, I can dimension the dice in many different shapes.

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:48.770
Like I need you to tell me that!

00:13:49.080 --> 00:13:50.910
Then I'll show you.

00:13:51.790 --> 00:13:53.070
Dimension Dice!

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.200
Oh no!  I didn't expect that shape!

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:06.570
Here I go.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:08.590
I summon Dark Magician!

00:14:09.830 --> 00:14:10.790
Dark Magician?

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:12.620
Can it be?

00:14:14.320 --> 00:14:20.020
Otogi-boy, I made some improvements to this game.

00:14:20.020 --> 00:14:21.470
Is that acceptable?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:24.410
Yes.  But what were they?

00:14:24.600 --> 00:14:28.640
I linked it to Duel Monsters.

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:36.280
New monsters have effects that will make Dungeon Dice Monsters a perfect game.

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.400
New monsters?

00:14:38.400 --> 00:14:39.720
What are they?

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:45.550
It's a secret, but you'll find out as you play the game.

00:14:46.660 --> 00:14:51.330
Dark Magician wasn't included in the original version that I made.

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:56.270
This must be a new monster that has effects that Pegasus mentioned.

00:14:59.420 --> 00:15:03.600
If it uses effects from Duel Monsters, then it's very dangerous!

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:09.750
I didn't inspect all the new monsters because I wanted to be surprised, but that could be my downfall.

00:15:10.080 --> 00:15:12.820
I move Dark Magician forward!

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.370
Here I go!

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:17.400
Dark Magician attacks Orgoth the Relentless!

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:20.970
Black Magic!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:34.740
Yeah!  Nice!

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:38.110
All right!  You destroyed Otogi's main monster!

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:41.310
- No!  Poor Otogi!

00:15:38.110 --> 00:15:41.310
- Yeah!  Nice, Yugi!

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:46.650
In that case, I'll defeat him before he accumulates more crests.

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.590
I have the perfect ace up my sleeve!

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:51.190
Dice roll!

00:15:55.820 --> 00:15:57.830
I move Dark Assailant!

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:10.130
And it will open the treasure chest.

00:16:13.550 --> 00:16:14.950
What is that?

00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:17.600
I'll save the surprise for later.

00:16:17.600 --> 00:16:19.350
It's your turn.

00:16:21.980 --> 00:16:25.590
The rare item Monster Cannon!

00:16:26.530 --> 00:16:28.080
Monster Cannon?

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.100
What's that?

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:53.580
Monster Cannon is a rare item that fires my monster to destroy your monster.

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.950
My target is Dark Magician!

00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.090
Monster Cannon, fire!

00:17:04.920 --> 00:17:08.250
I activate Dark Magician's effect!

00:17:08.560 --> 00:17:09.370
What?

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.480
Magical Hats!

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.310
Which one did Dark Magician hide under?

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.450
Monster Cannon!

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:26.560
Shoot the second Magical Hat from the left!

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:27.450
Fire!

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:31.200
Did I hit it?

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:47.050
It takes two Trap Crests to activate Magical Hats, but it can throw off your opponent's attack!

00:17:47.050 --> 00:17:49.270
Damn!  Yaranzo, retreat!

00:17:52.250 --> 00:17:55.900
Dark Magician must have other effects.

00:17:55.900 --> 00:17:57.720
I need to strengthen my defenses!

00:17:58.000 --> 00:17:59.550
I won't let you get away!

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:00.890
Dice roll!

00:18:03.120 --> 00:18:07.660
Dark Magician, use two Magic Crests to activate your effect!

00:18:08.510 --> 00:18:10.680
Mystic Box!

00:18:20.370 --> 00:18:22.940
This is the effect that Pegasus spoke of!

00:18:29.160 --> 00:18:30.080
Yaranzo!

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:39.160
My monsters are all destroyed!

00:18:39.980 --> 00:18:41.240
Impossible!

00:18:42.670 --> 00:18:45.150
Go, Dark Magician!

00:18:46.830 --> 00:18:48.430
Black Magic!

00:19:01.930 --> 00:19:03.480
He did it!

00:19:13.720 --> 00:19:15.660
It's all over.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:18.660
All my dreams are gone.

00:19:20.150 --> 00:19:27.370
I developed the game by myself so that I could achieve my Dungeon Dice Monsters dream.

00:19:27.880 --> 00:19:31.610
But now that my dream is gone, I have nothing left.

00:19:32.940 --> 00:19:34.570
That's not true.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.480
Dungeon Dice Monsters is a wonderful game.

00:19:37.650 --> 00:19:40.480
Yes.  That was a wonderful match.

00:19:40.480 --> 00:19:43.490
I was so excited that I didn't act my age.

00:19:43.580 --> 00:19:44.700
That's right.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:51.430
Just like Duel Monsters, everyone in the world will enjoy Dungeon Dice Monsters.

00:19:52.450 --> 00:19:54.730
Do you really think so?

00:19:54.730 --> 00:19:58.320
Yeah.  I don't like you, but I like this game.

00:19:58.320 --> 00:20:01.770
Yeah!  Teach me how to play too!

00:20:02.080 --> 00:20:03.080
Sure.

00:20:03.460 --> 00:20:07.750
As promised, you have to free Jonouchi.

00:20:08.120 --> 00:20:11.420
And I'll keep playing Duel Monsters.

00:20:11.840 --> 00:20:14.000
Of course, Yugi.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:17.370
I'm sorry I was so cruel to Jonouchi.

00:20:17.640 --> 00:20:25.510
Otogi, I don't believe games are for taking something from your opponent or creating hate.

00:20:25.510 --> 00:20:29.110
When two people have a great game, they become friends.

00:20:30.400 --> 00:20:34.710
Yugi, can I really become your friend?

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:37.840
Of course!

00:20:43.660 --> 00:20:44.800
You got mail?

00:20:44.860 --> 00:20:45.690
Yeah.

00:20:51.900 --> 00:20:57.630
Industrial Illusions wants to sign an official contract for Dungeon Dice Monsters!

00:20:58.000 --> 00:21:01.070
Hooray!  That's great, Otogi!

00:21:01.440 --> 00:21:03.000
That's great, Otogi.

00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:05.340
Thank you, Yugi.

00:21:05.560 --> 00:21:08.170
I'm sorry for calling you a cheater.

00:21:08.500 --> 00:21:10.110
Don't worry about it.

00:21:10.380 --> 00:21:12.430
You really are strong.

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:17.050
With a heart as strong as yours, I can see why you were able to defeat Pegasus.

00:21:17.050 --> 00:21:20.050
No, I didn't win because I was strong.

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:23.990
I won because I have great friends that support me.

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:27.400
And a great partner.

00:21:36.460 --> 00:21:37.910
Big trouble!

00:21:37.910 --> 00:21:42.220
A suspicious man in a black cloak steals Yugi's Millennium Puzzle!

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:48.310
Yugi believes that his other self is inside the Puzzle, so he must get it back!

00:21:48.710 --> 00:21:51.620
Yugi chases after the Puzzle to an abandoned buildilng.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:54.260
The man in the cloak challenges him to a duel.

00:21:54.260 --> 00:21:56.280
What's his goal?

00:21:56.570 --> 00:22:00.310
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Challenge from the Past
Terrifying Zera the Mant

00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:02.060
Duel, standby!

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:22.270
Even a long, long time ago

00:22:23.100 --> 00:22:27.640
I feel like I've been here

00:22:28.200 --> 00:22:37.320
The setting sun colors the classroom after school

00:22:37.640 --> 00:22:48.840
We all laugh as you point out that I cut my bangs too short

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:56.340
Time passes bit by bit

00:22:57.030 --> 00:23:01.610
The time when my bangs touch my eyelids

00:23:02.200 --> 00:23:06.720
Will never change

00:23:07.410 --> 00:23:11.990
The sunset envelops everyone

00:23:12.650 --> 00:23:17.190
To be who I am

00:23:17.820 --> 00:23:22.430
I've kept searching for something

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:27.140
The time that we're now spending together

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:30.070
I learned that's the answer

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:37.180
From now until forever...
